---
import { siteConfig } from "../lib/siteConfig";
---

<section
	class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20 lg:px-10"
	aria-labelledby="about-heading"
>
	<div class="reveal rounded-[2rem] bg-surface-card p-6 sm:p-10 lg:p-14">
		<h2 id="about-heading" class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink sm:text-3xl">
			About Bull or Bear
		</h2>
		<div
			class="prose prose-neutral mt-6 max-w-none prose-headings:font-extrabold prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-headings:text-ink prose-p:leading-relaxed prose-p:text-body prose-a:font-semibold prose-a:text-primary prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline prose-strong:text-ink dark:prose-invert"
		>
			<p>
				<strong>Bull or Bear</strong> is an independent blogs and media platform for readers who want the full picture before deciding which way to lean — bull or bear. What began as a handful of finance blogs has grown into a wider home for <a href="/business/">business</a>, <a href="/personal-finance/">personal finance</a>, <a href="/politics/">politics</a>, <a href="/world/">world news</a>, SEO blogs, and <a href="/ai/">AI blogs</a>, tied together by the how-to guides that turn each topic into something actually useful. It's all written in plain, direct language and free of the jargon that usually gates this kind of writing — because markets, money, and the decisions around both move faster than most explainers can keep up with, and Bull or Bear exists to close that gap.
			</p>

			<h3>Personal Finance, Money Management, and the Best Credit Cards in India</h3>
			<p>
				Money management sits at the center of what we do. Our personal finance coverage runs from the fundamentals — budgeting, saving, debt, and the money psychology behind why people spend the way they do — through to hands-on tools that do the math for you. The free <a href="/calculators/sip-calculator/">SIP calculator</a> and <a href="/calculators/emi-calculator/">EMI calculator</a> on Bull or Bear are built specifically around how Indian investors and borrowers actually plan: monthly SIP goals, step-up contributions, home and car loan EMIs, and the interest cost most banks would rather you not calculate yourself. We also research and rank the <a href="/personal-finance/best-cashback-credit-cards-in-india-2026/">best credit cards in India</a> on a rolling basis, because reward terms and fee structures change often enough that a "best of" list from last year is frequently wrong today.
			</p>

			<h3>AI Blogs: Real AI Use, AI SEO, AI Business, and How to Earn Money Using AI</h3>
			<p>
				AI is the fastest-moving beat on the site, and we treat it as a money story as much as a technology one. Our AI blogs are built around real AI use rather than hype — how businesses are folding AI SEO and AI business workflows into everyday operations, what actually works when you automate a task versus when it quietly breaks, and how creators and freelancers are turning AI use into income. If you've searched how to earn money using AI, our guides walk through the specific tools, workflows, and money making tips that hold up in practice, not just in a thread screenshot. The goal is simple: help readers earn money from AI skills without pretending the shortcuts are simpler than they are.
			</p>

			<h3>Politics, World News, Lifestyle, and GenZ Blogs</h3>
			<p>
				Politics and world news get the same market-aware lens as everything else here: what changed, who it moves, and why your money should care. That same lens extends into our lifestyle and GenZ blogs territory, including travel blogs and food blogs written with a money angle — how a new generation of Indian earners actually budgets and spends on travel, food, and everyday purchases while building toward bigger financial goals. It's personal finance and business writing that assumes the reader is smart, broke or building wealth in equal measure, and allergic to condescension.
			</p>

			<h3>Gadget Reviews, Comparison Blogs, Infographics, and the Daily Quiz</h3>
			<p>
				On the tech side, Bull or Bear runs gadget review and gadget comparison coverage that cuts straight to whether something is worth your money, distilled further into standalone comparison blogs and <a href="/infographics/">infographics</a> built for skimming and sharing. Every story on the homepage pairs with a <a href="/#quiz-heading">Daily Quiz</a> and finance quiz — a two-minute way to check whether the story actually landed, and a small, low-stakes habit that keeps readers coming back daily.
			</p>

			<h3>Follow Bull or Bear Everywhere</h3>
			<p>
				None of this lives only on the website. Follow <a href={siteConfig.social.instagram} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@bullorbear_stories on Instagram</a> and find <a href={siteConfig.social.youtube} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BullOrBear on YouTube</a> for the same reporting in shorter, faster formats built for a scroll. Between the site, the daily quiz, and the socials, Bull or Bear publishes new blogs, <a href="/latest/">latest news</a>, and world news breakdowns every single week — so whichever way the market, or the argument, is leaning, you'll have read it here first.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
